<td>{{a:263207}}
<p><span>Coursework in the Earth &amp; Environmental Sciences at Lake Tahoe Community College is for students&nbsp;</span><span>who are interested in solving&nbsp;problems from an interdisciplinary perspective.</span></p>
<p><span>Understand the relationships between the natural and social sciences by using the scientific methods of observation, experimentation, and analysis. Deepen your knowledge of the natural&nbsp;world, and gain hands-on experience with advanced scientific tools. Understand the scientific basis for environmental decision making and the legal, economic, and political issues involved in&nbsp;management&nbsp;of the environment.</span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span><iframe style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/TjeNagLtQWQ" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe></span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span>Many courses emphasize exploration and the study of Lake Tahoe, a natural lab of outstanding beauty and richness. Coursework is designed to align with the major prep and transfer requirements at a variety of institutions. Students are encouraged to meet with a LTCC counselor to ensure that course and degree selections align with the specific transfer requirements of each institution.</span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span style="font-size: 24px;">Choose your program:</span></p>
